    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 - # network locations; # network members; level of inclusivity re clan and religious school of thought 
1.2 - # women supported to become female madrassa teachers and joining the network; % cases mediated by women
1.3 - # people trained; # of cases shared (identified, engaged, resolved) 
1.4 - # social dialogues held on specific topics concerning good governance at existing network locations; analysis of level of inclusivity and consensus reached between representatives of different religious schools of thought 
1.5 - # of messages disseminated by ulema network on peace, dialogue, and good governance; # of AS responses or positions received
1.6 - # of religious leaders joining the network in new locations; # of new locations conducting social dialogues; # of community priorities identified and assisted; # of peace islands created and sustained 
2.1 - # of dugsi and madrassa curricula developed; # of network members and teachers trained on peace curriculum; % of increase in pupils&#x2019; knowledge of Islamic peace education 
2.2 - # of mothers with children who joined AS engaged into the intervention; # of audio messages of mothers recorded and disseminated 
2.3 - # of ulema trained on the religious counselling manual; # of prison and defectors centers visits conducted and Friday sermons delivered 
3.1 - # of women and religious leaders sensitized and trained on impact of trauma on society and Islamic Trauma Healing responses; # of Women MHPSS community support groups and religious leaders-led community MHPSS sessions held; # of survivors of exorcism rituals&#x2019; stories recorded and disseminated 
3.2 - # of Duca and Quran readings for AS victims to commemorate the 14th of October; # of cafis platforms convened to share AS-related stories and seek community forgiveness; # of victims/survivors&#x2019; and perpetrators&#x2019; stories shared via community radio  
3.3 - # of religious sites damaged / destroyed by AS identified and  rebuilt / renovated; # of forgiveness prayers held; % pro</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 -  198 network members (174 male/24 female), 16 network locations
1.2 - 24 female network members, 20 madrassa teachers, currently 12% women in ulema network 
1.3 - 7 trainings (1 Mog, 5 FMS, 1 WPS) for total 218 religious actors; 1 Experience sharing workshop (169 cases identified, 131 mediated) 
1.4 - Religious actors marginalized in Somali statebuilding: no official platforms for social-religious dialogue on good governance
1.5 - No standardized Friday sermons; peaceful Islamic key messages developed; 1 documentary in response to AS
1.6 - Network present in 1 pilot location of newly recovered areas (Awdheegle)
2.1 - 1 draft dugsi peace curriculum developed; 60 ulema network members trained on the peace curriculum; 20 female madrassa teachers trained on the peace curriculum; 20 dugsis in 4 FMS held and recorded Ramadan competitions in 2022; No madrassa peace curriculum prepared 
2.2 - Anecdotal evidence of children disappearing from dugsis and madrassas through AS recruitment
2.3 - 1 Draft Manual developed; anecdotal evidence that prison mosques are run by AS prisoners and used for recruitment; 3 prison breaks (Bossasso, Mogadishu, Galkayo) with AS inside job involvement  
3.1 - No community response for mental health challenges exist; Jinni exorcisms prevalent
3.2 - No community forums for social healing exist; Both formal and informal defection pathways with limited community buy-in and reintegration focus
3.3 - Mosques destroyed by AS identified in Awdeegle (1 &#x2013; requires rebuilding) and in Bahdo (1 &#x2013; requires renovation); communities unable to rebuild the religious sites themselves 
3.4 - Fatwa on eligibility of victims of AS attacks for zakat-giving issued; Piloted in 3 FMS locations (Bardhere, Kismayo, Jowhar); Ulema network identified victims and mobilized business community to support 32 victims and their families through zakat; In 2020, MERA published interviews with 17 Zobe blast victims encouraging zakat-giving
3.5 - No government-led support mechan</narrative>
     </comment>
